222	    /**
223	     * Move a claim to a new status; a move its current status does not allow is refused. Opening a
224	     * claim gives it its next number (the sheet's next, or the next in its period while the sheet numbers per
225	     * period) and records who opened it; voiding it keeps its number, which is
226	     * never given again; settling it fixes its due: the figure a statement binds it to, else its amount
227	     * at the rate in force on its date of its person's grade in force on that date, as rates are now, with the late charge it has gained
228	     * added on top, so later rate changes leave it as it is. The user
229	     * who opened a claim, or last edited it, cannot settle it, and a clerk settling it when that due is above the sheet's clerk limit
230	     * makes it PENDING instead, for a steward to approve or reject (a claim with no due is within any limit); a
231	     * steward settles anything. Opening, settling and voiding are each refused for a role the sheet's permission
232	     * matrix does not allow. Only a steward may void a SETTLED claim, and only within {@value #SETTLED_VOID_DAYS}
233	     * days of the day its log records it settled, by the sheet's today; its frozen figure then leaves every total
234	     * and the audit line ends with it as reversed. A claim due by inside a closed period cannot move. The sheet is locked
235	     * first, so moves on one sheet are made one at a time and no number is given twice.
236	     */
237	    @Transactional
238	    public Claim changeStatus(String sheetId, String user, long id, ClaimStatus next) {
239	        return changeStatus(sheetId, user, id, next, null);
240	    }
